{"name":"Grey Embrace","hex":"#b0bfb6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"embrace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clasp (someone or each other) in the arms with affection; to take in the arms; to hug.","To seize (something) eagerly or with alacrity; to accept or take up with cordiality; to welcome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of putting arms around someone and bringing the person close to the chest; a hug.","An enclosure partially or fully surrounding someone or something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Embrace (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Embrace is a 2016 Australian documentary film directed by Taryn Brumfitt. It concerns women's body image and is a response to surveys showing that 90% of women are \"highly dissatisfied\" with their bodies. It includes interviews with Mia Freedman, editor of the Australian Cosmopolitan and television talk-show hosts Amanda de Cadenet and Ricki Lake."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Embrace_2016_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embrace_(film)","wikidata":"Q24628873"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbn